IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcr-dates`

-- Workers Compensation Regulation 2016 (NSW) -- the claims procedure a claimant meets: Part 8 (notices, reports, internal
-- review), Part 9 (medical reports), Part 17 Division 3 Subdivision 2 (who pays the costs of a work injury damages case),
-- cl 168 (costs of a medical assessment) and cl 175(2) (overlapping certificates of capacity).
--
-- SEAT. The injured worker (for work injury damages, the claimant). Provisions addressed to the insurer, the employer, a
-- medical assessor or the court are encoded as what they mean for the worker: what must be in a notice, what must be
-- sent, what may be admitted, what can be recovered, who pays.
--
-- ANSWERS. JUST FALSE where the text's own words say no; NOTHING, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment, where it does not
-- answer on the facts given. Questions phrased "Does clause N stop me ...?" answer for that clause only.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Parts 8, 9 and 17 -- the claims procedure`

§§ `cl 37 -- notice of hearing loss`

DECLARE `Hearing loss notice goes to` IS ONE OF
    `my current employer, in whose employment the loss arose`
    `the last employer in whose employment the loss arose`
    `clause 37 does not apply`

-- cl 37(1) "If an injury is a loss, or further loss, of hearing that is of such a nature as to be caused by a gradual
-- process (including boilermaker's deafness ...) -- (a) notice of injury is to be given by the worker under section 61
-- of the 1998 Act -- (i) if the worker is employed by an employer in an employment to the nature of which the injury is
-- due -- to that employer, or (ii) if the worker is not so employed, to the last employer by whom the worker was employed
-- in an employment to the nature of which the injury is due, and (b) the notice must be in writing and be in the approved
-- form."
@export To which employer must I give notice of my gradual hearing loss (Regulation cl 37)? The notice must be in writing, in the approved form.
GIVEN `my hearing loss came on gradually` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your loss (or further loss) of hearing is of a kind caused by a gradual process, such as boilermaker's deafness or industrial deafness
      `I still work for an employer whose work caused it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are now employed by an employer in a kind of employment to whose nature the hearing loss is due
GIVETH A `Hearing loss notice goes to`
`To whom must I give notice of my hearing loss` MEANS
    IF `my hearing loss came on gradually`
    THEN IF `I still work for an employer whose work caused it`
         THEN `my current employer, in whose employment the loss arose`
         ELSE `the last employer in whose employment the loss arose`
    ELSE `clause 37 does not apply`

§§ `cll 38, 38A -- what a dispute notice must contain`

-- cl 38(1) A notice under s 78 of the 1998 Act "of an insurer's decision to dispute liability in respect of a claim or
-- any aspect of a claim (except in connection with a work injury damages matter), or to discontinue or reduce the amount
-- of weekly payments of compensation, is to contain the following information -- (a) ... (h)".
@export Does the insurer's notice disputing my claim, or stopping or reducing my weekly payments, contain everything clause 38 requires (Regulation cl 38(1))?
GIVEN `the notice disputes liability or stops or reduces my weekly payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice is of a decision to dispute liability for your claim or part of it (other than work injury damages), or to discontinue or reduce your weekly payments
      `it lists the documents I and my employer submitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Whether it identifies all the reports and documents you submitted with your claim and your employer submitted in connection with it
      `it lists every relevant report, for or against` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Whether it identifies all the reports relevant to the decision (medical reports, certificates, clinical notes, investigators' and rehabilitation reports and so on), whether or not they support the decision
      `it says the reports it must send are attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Whether it says that a copy of each report the insurer must provide comes with the notice
      `it explains how to ask for a review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (d) Whether it gives details of how to request a review of the decision
      `it says where I can get advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (e) Whether it says you can get advice or help from your union, a lawyer, the Independent Review Officer or another service set up by the Authority
      `it gives the Independent Review Officer's contact details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (f) Whether it gives the contact details of the Independent Review Officer
      `it gives the President's street and email addresses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (g) Whether it gives the street address and email address of the President (of the Personal Injury Commission)
      `it includes the approved-form summary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (h) Whether it includes a summary, in the approved form, of the effect of the decision, your review rights and how to ask for one, and the services that can help you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my dispute notice contain what clause 38 requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice disputes liability or stops or reduces my weekly payments`
    THEN IF     `it lists the documents I and my employer submitted`
            AND `it lists every relevant report, for or against`
            AND `it says the reports it must send are attached`
            AND `it explains how to ask for a review`
            AND `it says where I can get advice`
            AND `it gives the Independent Review Officer's contact details`
            AND `it gives the President's street and email addresses`
            AND `it includes the approved-form summary`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit with no "only": cl 38 covers those notices; cl 38A covers work injury damages)

-- cl 38A A notice under s 78 "of an insurer's decision to dispute liability in a work injury damages matter is to
-- contain the following information -- (a) ... (e)".
@export Does the insurer's notice disputing liability for my work injury damages claim contain everything clause 38A requires (Regulation cl 38A)?
GIVEN `it explains the pre-filing statement and mediation steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Whether it says that before you can start court proceedings you must first serve a pre-filing statement on the defendant (s 315) and then refer the claim to the Commission for mediation (s 318A)
      `it warns I cannot raise materially different matters in court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Whether it says you cannot raise matters in court that are materially different from those in your pre-filing statement, except with the court's leave
      `it lists the documents I submitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Whether it identifies all the reports and documents you submitted in making the claim
      `it says where I can get advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (d) Whether it says you can get advice or help from your union, a lawyer or a service set up by the Authority
      `it gives the President's or Principal Registrar's addresses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (e) Whether it gives the street and email address of the President or of the Principal Registrar of the District Court
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does my damages dispute notice contain what clause 38A requires` MEANS
        `it explains the pre-filing statement and mediation steps`
    AND `it warns I cannot raise materially different matters in court`
    AND `it lists the documents I submitted`
    AND `it says where I can get advice`
    AND `it gives the President's or Principal Registrar's addresses`

§§ `cl 41 -- copies of reports the insurer relies on`

DECLARE `Report kind` IS ONE OF
    `a medical report, including a report of an examination the employer required (s 119)`
    `a certificate of capacity`
    `clinical notes`
    `an investigator's report`
    `a workplace rehabilitation provider's report`
    `a health service provider's report`
    `another report with information relevant to the claim the dispute is about`
    `another kind of document`

DECLARE `Insurer decision` IS ONE OF
    `a decision to dispute liability for my claim or part of it`
    `a decision to discontinue or reduce my weekly payments`
    `a review decision confirming one of those decisions`
    `another decision`

DECLARE `Report copy` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer must give me a copy with the notice`
    `the insurer may give it to the doctor I nominate instead`
    `the insurer may give it to my lawyers instead`
    `it goes to whoever the Authority directs`
    `no copy is needed: I already have it and the notice identifies it`
    `clause 41 does not require a copy`

-- cl 41(1) the reports "that an employer or insurer has in [its] possession" -- (a)-(g); (2) the decisions (a)-(c); (3)
-- the employer or insurer "must provide a copy of any relevant report ... to the worker, as an attachment to a notice
-- ..., except where the report has already been supplied to the worker and that report is identified in a statement
-- under clause 38(1)(d)" (read as the statement of reports in cl 38(1)(b): finding 2, fork F11); (4) "any report that is
-- relevant to the claim or any aspect of the claim to which the decision relates, whether or not the report supports the
-- reasons"; (5) if of the opinion that supplying a copy "would pose a serious threat to the life or health of the worker
-- or any other person", it may instead supply "(a) ... a medical report, certificate of capacity or clinical notes -- to a
-- medical practitioner nominated by the worker ..., or (b) in any other case -- to a law practice representing the
-- worker"; (6) the Authority may direct otherwise.
@export Must the insurer send me a copy of this report with its decision notice, and if not to me, to whom (Regulation cl 41)?
GIVEN `the report` IS A `Report kind` @desc What the document is
      `the decision` IS AN `Insurer decision` @desc The decision the notice is about
      `the insurer or employer has the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer (or employer) has the report in its possession
      `the report is relevant to what was decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the report is relevant to the claim, or the part of it, that the decision is about (whether or not it supports the decision)
      `I already have it and the notice lists it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the report was already given to you and the notice's statement of reports identifies it
      `the insurer thinks a copy would seriously threaten someone's life or health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer or employer is of the opinion that giving you a copy would pose a serious threat to your life or health or anyone else's
      `the Authority has given a direction about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority (SIRA), on the insurer's application, has directed that the report go to someone else or be dealt with in another way
GIVETH A `Report copy`
`Must the insurer send me a copy of the report` MEANS
    IF `clause 41 reaches it`
    THEN IF `the Authority has given a direction about it`
         THEN `it goes to whoever the Authority directs`
         ELSE IF `I already have it and the notice lists it`
              THEN `no copy is needed: I already have it and the notice identifies it`
              ELSE IF `the insurer thinks a copy would seriously threaten someone's life or health`
                   THEN IF `it is medical`
                        THEN `the insurer may give it to the doctor I nominate instead`
                        ELSE `the insurer may give it to my lawyers instead`
                   ELSE `the insurer must give me a copy with the notice`
    ELSE `clause 41 does not require a copy`
    WHERE
        `clause 41 reaches it` MEANS
                `the insurer or employer has the report`
            AND `the report is relevant to what was decided`
            AND `the decision is one clause 41 covers`
            AND `the report is one clause 41 covers`
        `the decision is one clause 41 covers` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the decision`
            WHEN `another decision` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `the report is one clause 41 covers` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the report`
            WHEN `another kind of document` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `it is medical` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the report`
            WHEN `a medical report, including a report of an examination the employer required (s 119)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a certificate of capacity` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `clinical notes` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `cll 42A, 42B -- internal review by the insurer`

DECLARE `Review handling` IS ONE OF
    `my request does not meet clause 42A: it must be in writing`
    `the review was not dealt with as clause 42A requires`
    `the review was dealt with as clause 42A requires`

-- cl 42A(1) "A request under section 287A of the 1998 Act for a review of a decision of an insurer must be in writing."
-- (2) "The insurer must consider any relevant material submitted by the worker in connection with the request." (3) "The
-- request must not be dealt with by any person substantially involved in making the decision the subject of the
-- request."
@export Was my request for the insurer to review its decision made, and dealt with, as clause 42A requires (Regulation cl 42A)?
GIVEN `my request was in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked for the review in writing
      `the insurer considered the material I sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer considered the relevant material you submitted with the request
      `the reviewer helped make the original decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who dealt with your request was substantially involved in making the decision under review
GIVETH A `Review handling`
`Was my review dealt with as clause 42A requires` MEANS
    IF `my request was in writing`
    THEN IF `the insurer considered the material I sent` AND (NOT `the reviewer helped make the original decision`)
         THEN `the review was dealt with as clause 42A requires`
         ELSE `the review was not dealt with as clause 42A requires`
    ELSE `my request does not meet clause 42A: it must be in writing`

-- cl 42B A notice of the insurer's review decision is to "(a) be in writing, and (b) contain the information referred to
-- in clause 38(1), and (c) contain a concise and readily understandable statement of the reason for the insurer's
-- decision and of the issues relevant to the decision, and (d) identify any provision of the workers compensation
-- legislation on which the insurer relies".
@export Does the insurer's notice of its review decision contain everything clause 42B requires (Regulation cl 42B)?
GIVEN `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Whether the notice is in writing
      `it has everything clause 38(1) lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Whether it contains all the information a dispute notice must contain under clause 38(1) (documents, reports, review procedure, advice, contacts, approved-form summary)
      `it gives a clear statement of reasons and issues` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Whether it gives a concise and readily understandable statement of the reason for the decision and the issues relevant to it
      `it names the provisions relied on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (d) Whether it identifies the provisions of the workers compensation legislation the insurer relies on
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does my review decision notice contain what clause 42B requires` MEANS
        `it is in writing`
    AND `it has everything clause 38(1) lists`
    AND `it gives a clear statement of reasons and issues`
    AND `it names the provisions relied on`

§§ `Part 9 -- medical reports (cll 44-49)`

-- cl 44(4) "forensic medical report, in relation to a claim or dispute -- (a) means a report from a specialist medical
-- practitioner who has not treated the worker and that has been obtained for the purpose of proving or disproving an
-- entitlement, or the extent of an entitlement, in respect of the claim or dispute, and (b) includes a medical report
-- provided by a specialist medical practitioner in respect of an examination of the injured worker pursuant to section
-- 119 of the 1998 Act, and (c) does not include a report from a specialist medical practitioner who has not treated the
-- worker and that has been obtained for the purpose of proving or disproving an entitlement ... in respect of another
-- claim or dispute." (c) is applied before (b) (fork F12).
@export Is this report a "forensic medical report" in my claim or dispute, so that the one-report limit applies to it (Regulation cl 44(4))?
GIVEN `it is by a specialist medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the report is by a specialist medical practitioner
      `that specialist has treated me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that specialist has treated you
      `it was obtained to prove or disprove my entitlement in this claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was obtained to prove or disprove an entitlement (or its extent) in this claim or dispute
      `it was obtained for another claim or dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was obtained to prove or disprove an entitlement in another claim or dispute
      `it reports an examination my employer required (s 119)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it reports an examination of you that your employer required under s 119 of the 1998 Act
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is this a forensic medical report` MEANS
    IF `it is by a specialist medical practitioner`
    THEN IF (NOT `that specialist has treated me`) AND `it was obtained for another claim or dispute`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `it reports an examination my employer required (s 119)`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE IF (NOT `that specialist has treated me`) AND `it was obtained to prove or disprove my entitlement in this claim`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- cl 44(1) "only one forensic medical report may be admitted on behalf of a party to proceedings"; (3) "Where the injury
-- has involved treatment by more than one specialist medical practitioner, with different qualifications, then an
-- additional forensic medical report may be admitted from a medical practitioner with qualifications in that specialty."
-- "an additional" is read as one more report in all (fork F13; finding 3).
@export How many forensic medical reports may each side have admitted in my case before the Commission or the District Court (Regulation cl 44(1), (3))?
GIVEN `the number of different specialties that have treated me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many specialist medical practitioners with different qualifications (different specialties) have treated you for the injury (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many forensic medical reports may each side have admitted` MEANS
    IF `the number of different specialties that have treated me` GREATER THAN 1
    THEN 2
    ELSE 1

-- cl 45(1) "Despite clauses 44 and 46, a medical report other than the original report (a supplementary report) may be
-- admitted if -- (a) it has the purpose of clarifying the original report ... (b) ... updating the original report ...
-- (c) ... addressing issues omitted from the original report, or (d) ... addressing an opinion in the other party's
-- medical report." (3) "A supplementary report must have been provided by the medical practitioner who provided the
-- original report except when the medical practitioner has ceased (permanently or temporarily) to practise in the
-- specialty concerned, in which case the supplementary report must be provided by another medical practitioner of the
-- same specialty."
@export May my supplementary medical report be admitted despite the one-report limit (Regulation cl 45)?
GIVEN `it clarifies the original report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Whether its purpose is to clarify the original report (for example where the original was based on incomplete material), staying within the original report's scope
      `it updates the original report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Whether its purpose is to update the original by confirming, modifying or retracting an opinion in it
      `it covers issues the original left out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Whether its purpose is to address issues omitted from the original report
      `it answers the other side's report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (d) Whether its purpose is to address an opinion in the other party's medical report
      `the original author wrote it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was written by the doctor who wrote the original report
      `the original author has stopped practising in the specialty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that doctor has stopped (permanently or for now) practising in the specialty concerned
      `the writer is of the same specialty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If someone else wrote it, whether that doctor practises in the same specialty
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my supplementary report be admitted` MEANS
    IF `it has a permitted purpose` AND `it has the right author`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `it has a permitted purpose` MEANS
               `it clarifies the original report`
            OR `it updates the original report`
            OR `it covers issues the original left out`
            OR `it answers the other side's report`
        `it has the right author` MEANS
            IF `the original author has stopped practising in the specialty`
            THEN (NOT `the original author wrote it`) AND `the writer is of the same specialty`
            ELSE `the original author wrote it`

-- cl 46(1) "A forensic medical report must be disclosed to a medical assessor ... if any of the following occurs -- (a)
-- the report was admitted in proceedings on the claim or dispute, (b) no decision has been made as to whether or not the
-- report is to be admitted, and -- (i) the report was the report nominated by the claimant or respondent as the report
-- that [they] would introduce into evidence ..., or (ii) the report was the sole report in the particular specialty
-- concerned that was lodged ..., (c) the medical assessor calls for the production of the report under section
-- 324(1)(b)". (2) "is not to be disclosed ... otherwise than in accordance with this clause." (3) "Nothing in this clause
-- permits more than one forensic medical report of the type referred to in clause 44 to be disclosed to a medical
-- assessor on behalf of a party" (finding 3; fork F14).
@export Must my forensic medical report be given to the medical assessor (Regulation cl 46)? A no means it must not be disclosed to the assessor.
GIVEN `it was admitted in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the report was admitted in the proceedings on your claim or dispute
      `admission has been decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a decision has been made whether to admit the report
      `I nominated it as my report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you nominated it as the report you would put into evidence
      `it is the only report of its specialty I lodged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was the only report in that specialty that you lodged
      `the assessor called for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the medical assessor called for the report to be produced (s 324(1)(b) of the 1998 Act)
      `another of my forensic reports has gone to the assessor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another forensic medical report on your behalf has already been disclosed to the medical assessor
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my forensic report go to the medical assessor` MEANS
    IF `another of my forensic reports has gone to the assessor`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF    `it was admitted in the proceedings`
            OR ((NOT `admission has been decided`) AND (`I nominated it as my report` OR `it is the only report of its specialty I lodged`))
            OR `the assessor called for it`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- cl 47(1) "A party to proceedings on a claim is not entitled to be paid for or recover the cost of a medical report in
-- connection with the claim unless -- (a) the report has been admitted into those proceedings on behalf of the party, or
-- (b) the report has been disclosed to a medical assessor." (2) Where no proceedings have been taken, not entitled "unless
-- the report has been served on another party, and -- (a) the report would be admissible in proceedings on behalf of the
-- party, or (b) the report could be disclosed to a medical assessor." cl 48 "This Part does not affect any entitlement of
-- an injured worker to be paid for or recover the cost of obtaining medical treatment." cl 49 Part 9 does not apply to a
-- medical assessor's report under Part 7 of Chapter 7.
@export Does clause 47 stop me recovering the cost of my medical report (Regulation cll 47-49)? A no means clause 47 does not stop it; other rules decide how much.
GIVEN `the report is part of my medical treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cost is a cost of obtaining medical treatment (cl 48), not of a report for the claim
      `the report is a medical assessor's report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a report by a medical assessor under Part 7 of Chapter 7 of the 1998 Act (cl 49)
      `proceedings have been taken on my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether proceedings on your claim have been taken in the Commission or the District Court (including proceedings about provisional weekly payments)
      `it was admitted for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there are proceedings, whether the report was admitted in them on your behalf
      `it was disclosed to a medical assessor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there are proceedings, whether the report has been disclosed to a medical assessor
      `I served it on another party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there are no proceedings, whether you served the report on another party
      `it would be admissible or could go to an assessor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there are no proceedings, whether the report would be admissible on your behalf or could be disclosed to a medical assessor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does clause 47 stop me recovering the cost of my report` MEANS
    IF `the report is part of my medical treatment` OR `the report is a medical assessor's report`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE IF `proceedings have been taken on my claim`
         THEN (NOT (`it was admitted for me` OR `it was disclosed to a medical assessor`))
         ELSE (NOT (`I served it on another party` AND `it would be admissible or could go to an assessor`))

§§ `cl 168 -- costs of a medical assessment`

DECLARE `Assessment cost` IS ONE OF
    `the costs of the medical assessment`
    `the costs of a further examination for that assessment`
    `the costs of an appeal against the assessment`
    `the costs of a further hearing on that appeal`

-- cl 168(1) the employer or insurer need not pay "(a) a medical assessment ..., if the worker failed without reasonable
-- excuse to submit himself or herself to a medical examination conducted for the assessment, (b) any further examination
-- conducted for a medical assessment referred to in paragraph (a), (c) an appeal against such a medical assessment, if
-- the worker failed without reasonable excuse to attend a hearing on the appeal, (d) any further hearing held on an
-- appeal referred to in paragraph (c)." (2) "The worker is required to pay any costs of assessment referred to in
-- subclause (1)(a)-(d)." Whether an excuse is reasonable is asked as a fact.
@export Must I pay these costs of a medical assessment myself, because I missed the examination or the appeal hearing (Regulation cl 168)?
GIVEN `the costs` IS AN `Assessment cost` @desc Which costs: of the medical assessment, of a further examination for it, of an appeal against it, or of a further hearing on the appeal
      `I missed the examination for the assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to submit to the medical examination conducted for the assessment
      `I missed the appeal hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to attend a hearing on an appeal against the assessment
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a reasonable excuse for missing it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I pay the costs of the medical assessment` MEANS
    IF `I had a reasonable excuse`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: with a reasonable excuse cl 168 does not apply; who pays is for s 330 of the 1998 Act)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the costs`
         WHEN `the costs of the medical assessment` THEN `if missed` `I missed the examination for the assessment`
         WHEN `the costs of a further examination for that assessment` THEN `if missed` `I missed the examination for the assessment`
         WHEN `the costs of an appeal against the assessment` THEN `if missed` `I missed the appeal hearing`
         WHEN `the costs of a further hearing on that appeal` THEN `if missed` `I missed the appeal hearing`
    WHERE
        GIVEN `missed` IS A BOOLEAN
        GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
        `if missed` `missed` MEANS
            IF `missed`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: cl 168 does not apply; s 330 of the 1998 Act)

§§ `cll 94-99 -- who pays the costs of a work injury damages case`

DECLARE `Damages costs order` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer must pay my costs, on a party and party basis (cl 94)`
    `I must pay the insurer's costs, on a party and party basis (cl 95)`
    `each side bears its own costs (cl 96)`
    `the court's rules decide: ancillary proceedings (cl 98)`

-- cl 94: judgment "no less favourable to the claimant than the terms of the claimant's final offer of settlement in
-- mediation ... as certified by the mediator" -- the court "is to order the insurer to pay the claimant's costs". cl 95(1):
-- judgment "less favourable ... than the terms of the insurer's final offer" -- the claimant pays the insurer's costs;
-- (2) no order or judgment (the insurer has no liability) -- the claimant pays the insurer's costs. cl 96 otherwise each
-- side bears its own. cl 97(1): the insurer "wholly denies liability", "no mediation occurs" and the claimant obtains
-- judgment -- as if the insurer offered $0 and the claimant offered "(i) where the President issued a certificate ...
-- and the claimant, within one month of the issue of that certificate, made a subsequent offer ... -- the amount of
-- damages specified in that subsequent offer ..., or (ii) in any other case -- the amount of damages specified in the
-- pre-filing statement". (2): wholly denied, mediation without settlement -- the claimant's offer is a subsequent offer
-- "within one month of the conclusion of that mediation", or else the certified final offer. cl 98: not for ancillary
-- proceedings. cl 99: with two or more defendants who may have contribution or indemnity rights, an offer counts only if
-- the claimant's is made to all and settles against all, and an offer to the claimant settles against all and, where two
-- or more defendants make it, binds them jointly or jointly and severally for the whole.
-- Offers and judgments are compared by amount of damages (fork F15); cl 94 is applied before cl 95 (fork F16).
@export Who pays the legal costs of my court case for work injury damages (Regulation cll 94-99)?
GIVEN `the proceedings are ancillary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs are of proceedings ancillary to the claim (for example an interlocutory application), not of the claim itself
      `I obtained judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court gave you an order or judgment on the claim (no if it found the insurer not liable)
      `the damages awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the order or judgment, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the insurer wholly denied liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer wholly denied liability for the claim
      `the claim went to mediation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim was referred to mediation and mediation took place
      `the day mediation concluded` IS A DATE @desc The day the mediation concluded (any date if none)
      `the mediator certified my final offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mediator certified your final offer of settlement (s 318B of the 1998 Act)
      `my certified final offer` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of your certified final offer, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the mediator certified the insurer's final offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mediator certified the insurer's final offer of settlement
      `the insurer's certified final offer` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the insurer's certified final offer, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the President certified the denial and no mediation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the President issued a certificate verifying that the insurer wholly denied liability and that no mediation occurred
      `the day of the President's certificate` IS A DATE @desc The day that certificate was issued (any date if none)
      `I made a later offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made the insurer a subsequent offer of settlement after that certificate or after the mediation
      `the day of my later offer` IS A DATE @desc The day of that subsequent offer (any date if none)
      `my later offer` IS A NUMBER @desc The damages in that subsequent offer, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the damages in my pre-filing statement` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of damages in the pre-filing statement you served (s 315), in dollars
      `there are several defendants who may share liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether two or more defendants are said to be jointly (or jointly and severally) liable to you, with rights of contribution or indemnity between them
      `my offers went to all defendants to settle against all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether your offers were made to all the defendants to settle the claim against all of them
      `the insurer's offer settles against all and binds its makers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the offer made to you was to settle against all the defendants, and (if made by two or more) made them liable for the whole amount
GIVETH A `Damages costs order`
`Who pays the costs of my damages case` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are ancillary`
    THEN `the court's rules decide: ancillary proceedings (cl 98)`
    ELSE IF (NOT `I obtained judgment`)
         THEN `I must pay the insurer's costs, on a party and party basis (cl 95)`
         ELSE IF `my offer counts` AND (`the damages awarded` AT LEAST `my offer`)
              THEN `the insurer must pay my costs, on a party and party basis (cl 94)`
              ELSE IF `the insurer's offer counts` AND (`the damages awarded` LESS THAN `the insurer's offer`)
                   THEN `I must pay the insurer's costs, on a party and party basis (cl 95)`
                   ELSE `each side bears its own costs (cl 96)`
    WHERE
        `my offers pass clause 99` MEANS
            IF `there are several defendants who may share liability`
            THEN `my offers went to all defendants to settle against all`
            ELSE TRUE
        `the insurer's offers pass clause 99` MEANS
            IF `there are several defendants who may share liability`
            THEN `the insurer's offer settles against all and binds its makers`
            ELSE TRUE
        `a later offer within a month of` MEANS
            GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
            YIELD     `I made a later offer`
                  AND `the start` `falls on or before` `the day of my later offer`
                  AND `the day of my later offer` `falls on or before` (`the day` 1 `months after` `the start`)
        `deemed under 97(1)` MEANS `the insurer wholly denied liability` AND (NOT `the claim went to mediation`)
        `deemed under 97(2)` MEANS `the insurer wholly denied liability` AND `the claim went to mediation`
        `my offer counts` MEANS
            IF `deemed under 97(1)`
            THEN `my offers pass clause 99`
            ELSE IF `deemed under 97(2)`
                 THEN `my offers pass clause 99` AND (`a later offer within a month of` `the day mediation concluded` OR `the mediator certified my final offer`)
                 ELSE `my offers pass clause 99` AND `the mediator certified my final offer`
        `my offer` MEANS
            IF `deemed under 97(1)`
            THEN IF `the President certified the denial and no mediation` AND `a later offer within a month of` `the day of the President's certificate`
                 THEN `my later offer`
                 ELSE `the damages in my pre-filing statement`
            ELSE IF `deemed under 97(2)` AND `a later offer within a month of` `the day mediation concluded`
                 THEN `my later offer`
                 ELSE `my certified final offer`
        `the insurer's offer counts` MEANS
            IF `the insurer wholly denied liability`
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE `the insurer's offers pass clause 99` AND `the mediator certified the insurer's final offer`
        `the insurer's offer` MEANS
            IF `the insurer wholly denied liability`
            THEN 0
            ELSE `the insurer's certified final offer`

§§ `cl 175(2) -- overlapping certificates of capacity`

DECLARE `Governing certificate` IS ONE OF
    `the later certificate`
    `the earlier certificate`
    `neither certificate covers the day`

-- cl 175(2) "If a subsequent certificate covers a period that overlaps wholly or in part with a period covered by an
-- earlier certificate, the later certificate prevails for the whole of the period covered by the later certificate except
-- to the extent that the later certificate relates to a period before the later certificate was provided."
@export Which of two overlapping certificates of capacity governs a given day (Regulation cl 175(2))?
GIVEN `the earlier certificate's first day` IS A DATE @desc The first day the earlier certificate covers
      `the earlier certificate's last day` IS A DATE @desc The last day the earlier certificate covers
      `the later certificate's first day` IS A DATE @desc The first day the later certificate covers
      `the later certificate's last day` IS A DATE @desc The last day the later certificate covers
      `the day the later certificate was provided` IS A DATE @desc The day the later certificate was provided
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you want to know about
GIVETH A `Governing certificate`
`Which certificate governs the day` MEANS
    IF     `the later certificate's first day` `falls on or before` `the day asked about`
       AND `the day asked about` `falls on or before` `the later certificate's last day`
       AND (    `the day the later certificate was provided` `falls on or before` `the day asked about`
            OR (NOT `the earlier covers the day`))
    THEN `the later certificate`
    ELSE IF `the earlier covers the day`
         THEN `the earlier certificate`
         ELSE `neither certificate covers the day`
    WHERE
        `the earlier covers the day` MEANS
                `the earlier certificate's first day` `falls on or before` `the day asked about`
            AND `the day asked about` `falls on or before` `the earlier certificate's last day`
